// Prints a short summary of the two topics from steps 4 and 5 of the work order.

main() {
    println("=== Functions and roles of an IDE ===")
    println("An integrated development environment (IDE) puts the tools a developer needs in one place:")
    println("- a code editor with syntax highlighting and auto-completion")
    println("- project and file management")
    println("- building (compiling) and running the program")
    println("- debugging and an integrated terminal")
    println("")
    println("=== Programming languages and compilers ===")
    println("A programming language lets developers write instructions in a form humans can read.")
    println("A computer only runs machine code, so a compiler translates the source code")
    println("into machine code before the program can be executed.")
    println("Without a compiler, code written in a language like Cangjie cannot run.")
}
